  "name": "Eastern Bering Sea Survey: King and Tanner Crab",
  "description": "An annual trawl survey is conducted in the eastern Bering Sea to provide information on the distribution and abundance of four species of crabs - red king crab, blue king crab, and two species of Tanner crab. This information is provided to fishermen and processors as an aid in locating productive areas and judging the overall availability of crabs. Survey derived information is also used as part of the basis for management decisions. An additional report dealing with king crabs was released in September, 1978. [Reference: OTTO, R. S., R. A. MacINTOSH, A. K. FUKUYAMA, T. M. ARMETTA, and C.J. PACE. 1979. Report to industry on 1979 eastern Bering Sea survey King and Tanner crab. NWAFC Processed Rep. 79-14, 54 p. Northwest and Alaska Fish. Cent., Natl. Mar. Fish. Serv., NOAA, Kodiak Facility PO Box 1638, Kodiak, AK 99615.]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To report survey results of King and Tanner crab.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23564081",
